{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createHotkeyRecorder(options): SolidHotkeyRecorder;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHotkeyRecorder.ts#L61","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createHotkeyRecorder.ts:61"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SolidJS primitive for recording keyboard shortcuts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This primitive provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This primitive uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe\nto the recorder's store state (same pattern as useHotkeyRecorder in React)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" | (() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration options for the recorder (or accessor function)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SolidHotkeyRecorder.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SolidHotkeyRecorder"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object with recording state signals and control functions"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = createSignal<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = createHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording() ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      <Show when={recorder.recordedHotkey()}>\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey()}</div>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeyRecorder(options): SolidHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createHotkeyRecorder.ts:61](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHotkeyRecorder.ts#L61)\n\nSolidJS primitive for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis primitive provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the recorder's store state (same pattern as useHotkeyRecorder in React).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`HotkeyRecorderOptions` \\| (() => `HotkeyRecorderOptions`)\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder (or accessor function)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SolidHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/SolidHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state signals and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = createSignal<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = createHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording() ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      <Show when={recorder.recordedHotkey()}>\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey()}</div>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createHotkeyRecorder\ntitle: createHotkeyRecorder\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeyRecorder(options): SolidHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createHotkeyRecorder.ts:61](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHotkeyRecorder.ts#L61)\n\nSolidJS primitive for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis primitive provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the recorder's store state (same pattern as useHotkeyRecorder in React).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`HotkeyRecorderOptions` \\| (() => `HotkeyRecorderOptions`)\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder (or accessor function)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SolidHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/SolidHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state signals and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = createSignal<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = createHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording() ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      <Show when={recorder.recordedHotkey()}>\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey()}</div>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
